cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
title: >-
  Risk-Controlled Applicability Set Retrieval (RCASR) for Regulation-Grounded
  Construction-Site Visual Screening
  — code, frozen configurations, analysis plans and aggregate results (ARGus)
abstract: >-
  Code and evaluation artifacts for Risk-Controlled Applicability Set Retrieval
  (RCASR). Screening a site photograph against a regulation library first requires
  deciding which provisions apply. RCASR frames this as set prediction under
  asymmetric miss/exposure cost: it re-weights a retrieval prior by the probability
  that each provision's compiled subject and state conditions hold, computed from
  token-level posteriors over 131 rule-agnostic visual atoms with abstention, and
  selects a set at a target mean width or under conformal risk control. Includes the
  frozen runtime configurations, pre-specified analysis plans, SHA-256 input
  snapshots and the aggregate results behind every table, on top of the ARGus
  screening framework of the earlier study (releases v1.x).
